    "content": "Ahmed Shide, who served as Ethiopia's Minister of Finance since 2018, was elected Speaker of the House of Peoples' Representatives on [date]. The election took place as the new parliamentary session opened in Addis Ababa. Shide, a long-serving member of the federal government, had been a member of parliament representing the Somali region of Ethiopia.\n\nDuring his tenure as Finance Minister, Shide played a key role in shaping Ethiopia's economic policies and implementing financial reforms. His appointment as Speaker comes amid ongoing political and economic changes in the country. The House of Peoples' Representatives is the lower chamber of Ethiopia's bicameral parliament and holds significant legislative power.\n\nShide's election is notable given his background from the Somali region, one of Ethiopia's nine regional states. He has been a prominent figure in Ethiopian politics, bridging regional and federal roles. His experience in finance and governance is expected to influence the legislative agenda as the government addresses economic challenges and development priorities.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, Shide's rise to a top parliamentary position is significant. It underscores the political participation of ethnic Somalis within Ethiopia's federal system. Many diaspora Somalis maintain close ties to the Somali region and follow Ethiopian political developments closely, as they impact cross-border relations, trade, and security. Shide's new role may also elevate the profile of Somali region issues in national debates.\n\nThe appointment comes at a time when Ethiopia is navigating complex domestic and regional dynamics, including economic reforms and security concerns. As Speaker, Shide will oversee parliamentary proceedings and play a part in shaping legislation. His financial expertise may be particularly relevant as the government seeks to stabilize the economy and attract investment.\n\nObservers will watch how Shide balances his new responsibilities with the expectations of his constituency and the broader Somali community. His election reflects the evolving political landscape in Ethiopia, where regional representation and federal unity remain key themes.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/05/axmed-shide-oo-loo-doortay-guddoomiyaha-baarlamaanka-itoobiya/",
